==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|ru|cu|кратъ}}, from {{der|ru|sla-pro|*kortъ}}. Cognate with {{cog|sh|-кра̄т}} (e.g. {{m|sh|два́кра̄т||twice}}), {{cog|sl|kràt}} (gen. {{m|sl|kráta}}), {{cog|cs|-krát}} (e.g. {{m|cs|dvakrát||twice}}), {{cog|sk|krát}}, {{cog|pl|-kroć}} (e.g. {{m|pl|dwakroć||twice}}), {{cog|hsb|-kroć}}, {{cog|dsb|-krot}}. More distantly cognate with {{cog|lt|kar̃tas||[[time]], [[occurrence]]}} (plural {{m|lt|kartaĩ}}), {{m|lt|kartà||[[layer]], [[row]]}} (acc. {{m|lt|kar̃tą}}), {{cog|lv|kā̀rtа||[[layer]], [[row]]}}, {{cog|sa|सकृत्|tr=sakṛ́t|t=once}}, {{m|sa|कृत्वस्|tr=kṛ́tvas|t=times, occurrences|g=p}}, {{cog|ae|𐬵𐬀𐬐𐬆𐬭𐬆𐬝|t=once}}. Vasmer suggests that these terms are cognate with {{cog|lt|kir̃sti||to [[chop]]}} (1sg. {{m|lt|kertù}}), and notes the parallelism with {{ncog|ru|раз}} and {{m|ru|ре́зать||to [[cut]]}}, and {{ncog|lt|sỹkis||[[time]], [[occurrence]]}} and {{ncog|ru|секу́||I [[cut]], I [[chop]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|крат}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|крат|(2)}}

# {{lb|ru|dated}} [[time]], [[occurrence]], [[-fold]]
#: {{syn|ru|раз<q:the normal term>}}

====Usage notes====
* Although the base term itself is now dated, it is still found in the expression {{m|ru|во́ сто кра́т||a [[hundred]] [[times]]}} and in compounds such as {{m|ru|многокра́тный||[[multifold]], [[multiple]], [[manifold]]}}, {{m|ru|однокра́тный||[[single]]}}, {{m|ru|стокра́т||[[many]] [[times]]|pos=literary}}, etc.

